A main-thread command that wraps the append to the top-level .gitignore of the sandbox repo in a subshell, followed by a second command (ls x), must be DENIED. The allowed single append (bw_main_gitignore_worktrees_append_allow) is judged one segment at a time, and the subshell hides the outer segment count, so the wrapped form currently slips through the guard. Expected to FAIL today: the guard allows it, so stdout is empty instead of a deny JSON.
